    slug: 'how-image-generators-work', title: 'How AI Image Generators Work', track: 'ai', level: 'Beginner', poster: 1,
    summary: 'Diffusion models turn pure noise into a picture by removing a little noise at a time, guided by your text prompt.',
    scenes: [
      { kit: 'title', title: 'How AI Image Generators Work', sub: 'From pure noise to a picture', track: 'Artificial Intelligence', chapter: 'Introduction', say: 'Type a description and an AI draws it in seconds. Most of these image generators are diffusion models. Their trick sounds backwards: they create images by removing noise.' },
      { kit: 'diffusion', shape: 'heart', prompt: 'a pink heart icon', sub: 'illustration of the denoising process', chapter: 'Denoising', say: 'Generation starts with random static. At each step, the model predicts which part of the picture is noise and removes a little of it. Slowly, shapes appear, then details sharpen, until the image matches the prompt.' },
      { kit: 'pipeline', head: 'How the model learned', steps: ['Take real images', 'Add noise', 'Predict the noise', 'Repeat millions of times'], desc: ['Millions of images, each with a caption.', 'Add a random amount of noise to each image.', 'The network learns to guess exactly which noise was added.', 'Once it predicts noise well, running it in reverse creates new images.'], chapter: 'Training', say: 'During training, the model sees millions of captioned images. Noise is added to each one, and the network learns to predict exactly which noise was added. Once it is good at that, you can start from pure noise and run the process in reverse.' },
      { kit: 'diffusion', shape: 'smiley', prompt: 'a happy yellow face', head: 'The prompt steers every step', chapter: 'Guided by text', say: 'The text prompt is turned into embeddings, and they guide every denoising step. A different prompt, starting from the same kind of noise, ends in a different picture.' },
      { kit: 'bullets', head: 'Using image generators responsibly', items: ['Check the tool’s licence before commercial use', 'Do not imitate real people without consent', 'Watch for stereotypes in results', 'Label AI-generated images where appropriate'], chapter: 'Responsible use', say: 'Use these tools responsibly. Check licences, never create images of real people without consent, watch for stereotypes in the results, and label AI images when it matters.' },
      { kit: 'bullets', style: 'recap', items: ['Start from random noise', 'Remove a little predicted noise at every step', 'The text prompt guides each step', 'Trained by learning to predict added noise'], chapter: 'Recap', say: 'To recap. Diffusion starts from noise, removes a little predicted noise at every step, is guided by the prompt, and was trained by learning to predict the noise added to real images.' }
    ],
